  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that it is improper to narrow the scope of a stand\u2011alone general discrimination ban that does not identify specific practices."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The government argues that Congress created a limited scheme that gives full judicial remedies only to a small group of federal employees, leaving many others without any remedy."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, it is improper to narrow the scope of a general discrimination ban that does not identify specific practices."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 9,
                "start": 9
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, Congress could have added federal employers to the definition of \u201cemployer\u201d and applied the private\u2011sector regime, but instead created a stand\u2011alone prohibition."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 56,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Guerra, it makes no sense to give some employees remedies under one scheme while leaving others with none."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Guerra, employees who complain about age discrimination and are then fired in retaliation have no remedy."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Myrna Gomez\u2011P\u00e9rez)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, Congress decided to treat retaliation against federal workers who complain of age discrimination differently from other forms of retaliation, creating a four\u2011part patchwork scheme."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 45,
                "start": 45
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Garre, the \u201cany employee\u201d language in section\u202f623d shows that Congress intended the anti\u2011retaliation provision to cover all employees, not just those over 40."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Garre, the Age Discrimination and Employment Act does not expressly prohibit retaliation in the federal sector and should not be read to do so."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent (U.S. Government / Postmaster General)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
